  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study on Health in Humanitarian Settings</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Change has been identified as a threat multiplier and primary driver of disaster risk, migration, and humanitarian needs globally. This study, through Johns Hopkins University, aims to illustrate possible application of predictive capacity of population displacement and resulting operational considerations to improve response preparedness and capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
